<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title><%= pageTitle || 'Privacy Policy - ZenoPay' %></title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/header.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/footer.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/privacy.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/header') %>

  <section class="privacy-hero" aria-labelledby="privacy-page-title">
    <div class="privacy-hero-content">
      <div class="hero-icon-wrap" aria-hidden="true">
        <i class="fas fa-shield-halved hero-icon"></i>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">Data Protection</p>
      <h1 id="privacy-page-title" class="hero-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">How we collect, use, and protect your information</p>
      <div class="hero-meta" aria-label="Document metadata">
        <span class="meta-badge effective-badge">
          <i class="fas fa-calendar-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>Last Updated: January 29, 2026</span>
        </span>
        <span class="meta-badge version-badge">
          <i class="fas fa-code-branch" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>Version 2.0</span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main class="privacy-page-main">
    <div class="privacy-page">
      <div class="privacy-container">
        <button
          id="privacyMobileTocToggle"
          class="privacy-mobile-toc-toggle"
          type="button"
          aria-controls="privacyTocPanel"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-label="Toggle table of contents"
        >
          <i class="fas fa-list" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>Table of Contents</span>
        </button>

        <div class="privacy-layout">
          <!-- ===================================================
               SIDEBAR — sticky-safe
               align-items: start is set on .privacy-layout so
               this wrapper can be position:sticky without being
               stretched to grid-row height.
               No overflow on any ancestor of this element.
               =================================================== -->
          <aside class="privacy-toc-wrapper is-collapsed-mobile" id="privacyTocPanel" aria-label="Privacy Policy Table of Contents">
            <nav class="privacy-toc" aria-labelledby="privacyTocTitle">
              <div class="privacy-toc-header">
                <p class="privacy-toc-kicker">
                  <i class="fas fa-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                  Navigate
                </p>
                <h2 class="privacy-toc-title" id="privacyTocTitle">Privacy Policy Contents</h2>
              </div>

              <div class="privacy-toc-links">
                <a href="#section-1" class="toc-item toc-active" data-section="section-1" aria-current="true">
                  <span class="toc-num">1</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Introduction</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-2" class="toc-item" data-section="section-2">
                  <span class="toc-num">2</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Information We Collect</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-3" class="toc-item" data-section="section-3">
                  <span class="toc-num">3</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">How We Use Your Information</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-4" class="toc-item" data-section="section-4">
                  <span class="toc-num">4</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Information Sharing &amp; Disclosure</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-5" class="toc-item" data-section="section-5">
                  <span class="toc-num">5</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Data Security</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-6" class="toc-item" data-section="section-6">
                  <span class="toc-num">6</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-7" class="toc-item" data-section="section-7">
                  <span class="toc-num">7</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Your Rights &amp; Choices</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-8" class="toc-item" data-section="section-8">
                  <span class="toc-num">8</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Data Retention</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-9" class="toc-item" data-section="section-9">
                  <span class="toc-num">9</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">International Data Transfers</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-10" class="toc-item" data-section="section-10">
                  <span class="toc-num">10</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Children's Privacy</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-11" class="toc-item" data-section="section-11">
                  <span class="toc-num">11</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Changes to This Policy</span>
                </a>
                <a href="#section-12" class="toc-item" data-section="section-12">
                  <span class="toc-num">12</span>
                  <span class="toc-text">Contact Us</span>
                </a>
              </div>

              <div class="privacy-sidebar-actions">
                <button id="privacyPrintButton" class="action-btn" type="button" aria-label="Print Privacy Policy">
                  <i class="fas fa-print" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                  <span>Print</span>
                </button>
                <button id="privacyDownloadButton" class="action-btn action-btn-primary" type="button" aria-label="Download Privacy Policy PDF">
                  <i class="fas fa-download" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                  <span>Download PDF</span>
                </button>
              </div>
            </nav>
          </aside>

          <div class="privacy-content-shell">
            <article class="privacy-content" aria-label="Privacy Policy content">

              <!-- Section 1: Introduction -->
              <section id="section-1" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-1-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">1</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Overview</p>
                    <h2 id="section-1-title" class="section-title">Introduction</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>ZenoPay ("we," "us," or "our") is committed to protecting the privacy and security of your personal information. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, retain, and safeguard information when you access our websites, mobile applications, payment APIs, merchant dashboards, hosted payment pages, and related services (collectively, the "Services").</p>
                  <p>By using the Services, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to the practices described in this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree to these practices, please do not use our Services.</p>

                  <div class="callout-box info-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-circle-info callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Your Privacy Matters</strong>
                      ZenoPay processes personal data as both a data controller (when managing your ZenoPay account) and a data processor (when processing payments on behalf of merchants). This policy covers both roles.
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Scope of This Policy</h3>
                  <p>This Privacy Policy applies to all individuals who interact with ZenoPay, including registered users, merchants, API integrators, visitors to our websites, and recipients of ZenoPay-processed transactions. It does not cover the privacy practices of third-party services that you may access through links on our platform.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Regulatory Framework</h3>
                  <p>ZenoPay operates in compliance with applicable data protection laws, including but not limited to the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS), and local financial data protection requirements in the jurisdictions where we operate. Our data handling practices are designed to meet or exceed these standards.</p>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 2: Information We Collect -->
              <section id="section-2" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-2-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">2</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Data We Process</p>
                    <h2 id="section-2-title" class="section-title">Information We Collect</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>We collect different categories of information depending on how you interact with the Services. We only collect information that is necessary to provide, improve, and secure our Services.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Personal Information</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Full legal name, date of birth, and nationality</li>
                    <li>Email address, phone number, and mailing address</li>
                    <li>Government-issued ID numbers (passport, national ID, driving licence) collected during KYC verification</li>
                    <li>Facial biometric data or liveness check data for identity verification (where required by law)</li>
                    <li>Business registration details, beneficial ownership information, and director/officer records for merchant accounts</li>
                  </ul>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Financial Information</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Bank account numbers, sort codes, routing numbers, and IBAN details</li>
                    <li>Payment card numbers (stored in tokenized form only — we never store full PAN data)</li>
                    <li>Transaction history, payment amounts, currencies, timestamps, and counterparty details</li>
                    <li>Wallet balances, settlement records, refund data, and chargeback history</li>
                    <li>Tax identification numbers and VAT registration numbers where applicable</li>
                  </ul>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Technical Information</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li>IP address, device identifiers, browser fingerprint, and operating system</li>
                    <li>Session tokens, API keys, integration metadata, and webhook delivery logs</li>
                    <li>Geolocation data (country/region level) inferred from your IP address</li>
                    <li>Error logs, performance metrics, latency data, and system diagnostics</li>
                    <li>HTTP headers and referrer information associated with requests to our APIs</li>
                  </ul>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Behavioural &amp; Usage Information</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Pages visited, features used, and navigation paths within the platform</li>
                    <li>Search queries, filter selections, and dashboard interactions</li>
                    <li>Preference settings, notification choices, and communication history</li>
                    <li>Support tickets, chat transcripts, and feedback submissions</li>
                  </ul>

                  <div class="callout-box info-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-database callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Sensitive Data Notice</strong>
                      Some data we collect — such as government ID numbers, biometric identifiers, and financial account details — is classified as sensitive personal data under applicable law. We apply heightened protections to this category of information.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 3: How We Use Your Information -->
              <section id="section-3" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-3-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">3</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Purpose &amp; Legal Basis</p>
                    <h2 id="section-3-title" class="section-title">How We Use Your Information</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>We process your personal data only for specific, legitimate purposes and only to the extent necessary for those purposes. Our legal bases for processing include contractual necessity, legal obligation, legitimate interests, and your consent where required.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Service Delivery</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Creating, verifying, and maintaining your ZenoPay account</li>
                    <li>Processing payments, transfers, refunds, and settlement transactions</li>
                    <li>Authenticating your identity and authorizing access to the platform</li>
                    <li>Providing merchant tools, APIs, and payment infrastructure</li>
                    <li>Delivering transactional notifications, receipts, and statements</li>
                  </ul>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Security &amp; Fraud Prevention</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Detecting, investigating, and preventing fraudulent, unauthorized, or illegal activity</li>
                    <li>Performing sanctions screening and anti-money laundering (AML) checks</li>
                    <li>Evaluating transaction risk in real time using automated and manual review systems</li>
                    <li>Maintaining audit logs and security event records</li>
                  </ul>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Legal &amp; Regulatory Compliance</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Meeting KYC, AML, and Customer Due Diligence (CDD) obligations</li>
                    <li>Responding to lawful requests from financial regulators, law enforcement, and courts</li>
                    <li>Maintaining records required by payment network rules and financial regulations</li>
                  </ul>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Product Improvement &amp; Analytics</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Analysing usage patterns to improve platform reliability and usability</li>
                    <li>Conducting research and testing on new features and product enhancements</li>
                    <li>Generating aggregated, anonymized performance and market insights</li>
                  </ul>

                  <div class="callout-box warning-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Automated Decision-Making</strong>
                      ZenoPay uses automated systems to assess transaction risk, detect fraud, and screen for sanctions. These systems may result in a transaction being declined or an account being flagged for review. You have the right to request human review of significant automated decisions affecting you.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 4: Information Sharing -->
              <section id="section-4" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-4-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">4</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Third Parties</p>
                    <h2 id="section-4-title" class="section-title">Information Sharing &amp; Disclosure</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>ZenoPay does not sell your personal information to third parties. We share your data only in the circumstances described below, and always subject to appropriate contractual safeguards.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Payment Network Partners</h3>
                  <p>To process transactions, we share necessary payment data with card networks (Visa, Mastercard), acquiring banks, issuing banks, mobile money operators, and other payment rails required to complete your transaction. This data sharing is essential to provide the Services.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Service Providers &amp; Sub-Processors</h3>
                  <p>We engage trusted third-party vendors to support specific operational functions, including cloud infrastructure providers, identity verification services, fraud detection platforms, customer support tooling, and email delivery services. All sub-processors operate under binding data processing agreements with data minimization and security requirements.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Merchants</h3>
                  <p>If you are a payer completing a transaction through a ZenoPay-powered merchant checkout, we share limited transaction details (such as confirmation status and order reference) with that merchant. The merchant's own privacy policy governs their handling of your data independent of ZenoPay.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Regulatory &amp; Legal Disclosures</h3>
                  <p>We may disclose personal data to financial regulators, tax authorities, law enforcement agencies, and courts when required by applicable law or a valid legal process. Where permitted, we will notify you of such disclosures before complying.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Business Transfers</h3>
                  <p>In the event of a merger, acquisition, restructuring, or sale of all or part of our business, your personal data may be transferred as part of that transaction. We will provide advance notice and ensure continuity of privacy protections.</p>

                  <div class="callout-box info-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-handshake callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>No Sale of Personal Data</strong>
                      ZenoPay has never sold and will never sell your personal data to advertisers, data brokers, or marketing companies.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 5: Data Security -->
              <section id="section-5" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-5-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">5</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Protection Measures</p>
                    <h2 id="section-5-title" class="section-title">Data Security</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>Protecting your data is foundational to our business. ZenoPay implements a comprehensive, multi-layered security programme aligned with PCI DSS Level 1, ISO 27001, and SOC 2 Type II frameworks. Our security controls are continuously monitored, tested, and improved.</p>

                  <div class="security-highlights-card">
                    <div class="security-highlights-title">
                      <i class="fas fa-shield-halved" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                      Security Highlights
                    </div>
                    <div class="security-highlights-grid">
                      <div class="security-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-lock security-item-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <div>
                          <strong>Encryption at Rest</strong>
                          <p>All stored data is encrypted using AES-256. Database volumes, backups, and object storage are encrypted with customer-managed or provider-managed keys.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="security-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-arrow-right-arrow-left security-item-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <div>
                          <strong>Encryption in Transit</strong>
                          <p>All data in transit is protected by TLS 1.2 or higher. We enforce HSTS, certificate pinning on mobile clients, and mutual TLS for critical API endpoints.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="security-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-id-badge security-item-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <div>
                          <strong>Access Controls</strong>
                          <p>Role-based access control (RBAC), least-privilege principles, multi-factor authentication, and privileged access management govern all internal access to production systems.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="security-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-magnifying-glass security-item-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <div>
                          <strong>Continuous Monitoring</strong>
                          <p>24/7 security operations monitoring, anomaly detection, intrusion detection systems, and automated threat alerting are active across all environments.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="security-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-flask security-item-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <div>
                          <strong>Penetration Testing</strong>
                          <p>We conduct annual third-party penetration tests and maintain a coordinated vulnerability disclosure programme with responsive remediation SLAs.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="security-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-circle-check security-item-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        <div>
                          <strong>PCI DSS Compliance</strong>
                          <p>Card data is never stored in raw form. All card processing flows are certified to PCI DSS Level 1. Tokenization is used throughout.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Data Breach Response</h3>
                  <p>In the event of a personal data breach that poses a risk to affected individuals, ZenoPay will notify the relevant supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming aware and will communicate directly with affected users without undue delay, in compliance with GDPR Article 33 and applicable financial data protection requirements.</p>

                  <div class="callout-box warning-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Shared Responsibility</strong>
                      Security is a shared responsibility. You are accountable for protecting your account credentials, enabling two-factor authentication, and reporting suspicious activity promptly. ZenoPay will never ask for your password by email or phone.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 6: Cookies -->
              <section id="section-6" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-6-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">6</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Tracking Technologies</p>
                    <h2 id="section-6-title" class="section-title">Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>ZenoPay uses cookies and similar tracking technologies to operate the Services, enhance your experience, and analyse how our platform is used. This section explains what we set, why, and how you can manage your preferences.</p>

                  <div class="cookie-table-wrapper" role="region" aria-label="Cookie types table">
                    <table class="cookie-table">
                      <thead>
                        <tr>
                          <th scope="col">Cookie Type</th>
                          <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
                          <th scope="col">Retention</th>
                          <th scope="col">Required</th>
                        </tr>
                      </thead>
                      <tbody>
                        <tr>
                          <td><span class="cookie-badge cookie-essential">Essential</span></td>
                          <td>Session management, authentication tokens, CSRF protection, load balancing, and fraud detection signals essential to the secure operation of the Services.</td>
                          <td>Session / Up to 30 days</td>
                          <td><span class="cookie-required">Yes</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td><span class="cookie-badge cookie-functional">Functional</span></td>
                          <td>Remembering your language preference, dashboard layout, notification settings, and other UI personalisation choices.</td>
                          <td>Up to 1 year</td>
                          <td><span class="cookie-optional">Optional</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td><span class="cookie-badge cookie-analytics">Analytics</span></td>
                          <td>Measuring page views, feature usage, session duration, and performance metrics to improve the platform. We use privacy-preserving analytics with IP anonymisation.</td>
                          <td>Up to 13 months</td>
                          <td><span class="cookie-optional">Optional</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                          <td><span class="cookie-badge cookie-security">Security</span></td>
                          <td>Device fingerprinting, behavioural signals, and risk scoring used by our fraud prevention and anti-bot systems to protect transactions.</td>
                          <td>Up to 6 months</td>
                          <td><span class="cookie-required">Yes</span></td>
                        </tr>
                      </tbody>
                    </table>
                  </div>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Managing Cookie Preferences</h3>
                  <p>On your first visit to our website, you will be presented with a cookie consent banner where you can accept or decline optional cookie categories. You can update your preferences at any time through the "Cookie Settings" link in the website footer. Disabling non-essential cookies does not affect your ability to use core Services features.</p>

                  <p>You may also control cookies through your browser settings, though blocking all cookies may impair the functionality of certain pages and features.</p>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 7: Your Rights -->
              <section id="section-7" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-7-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">7</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Your Control</p>
                    <h2 id="section-7-title" class="section-title">Your Rights &amp; Choices</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have a range of rights regarding your personal information. ZenoPay respects these rights and provides accessible mechanisms to exercise them.</p>

                  <div class="rights-card" role="region" aria-label="Your privacy rights">
                    <div class="rights-card-header">
                      <i class="fas fa-user-shield" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                      <span>Your Privacy Rights</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="rights-grid">
                      <div class="right-item">
                        <div class="right-icon-wrap">
                          <i class="fas fa-eye" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="right-content">
                          <strong>Right of Access</strong>
                          <p>Request a copy of personal data we hold about you, including the purposes for which it is processed.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="right-item">
                        <div class="right-icon-wrap">
                          <i class="fas fa-pen-to-square" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="right-content">
                          <strong>Right to Correction</strong>
                          <p>Request that inaccurate or incomplete personal data we hold about you be corrected or updated.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="right-item">
                        <div class="right-icon-wrap">
                          <i class="fas fa-trash-can" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="right-content">
                          <strong>Right to Deletion</strong>
                          <p>Request erasure of your personal data where it is no longer necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, subject to legal and regulatory retention requirements.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="right-item">
                        <div class="right-icon-wrap">
                          <i class="fas fa-file-export" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="right-content">
                          <strong>Right to Portability</strong>
                          <p>Receive a structured, machine-readable export of your personal data to transfer to another service provider.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="right-item">
                        <div class="right-icon-wrap">
                          <i class="fas fa-ban" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="right-content">
                          <strong>Right to Object / Opt-Out</strong>
                          <p>Object to processing based on legitimate interests, opt out of marketing communications, or restrict processing pending a dispute about accuracy.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                      <div class="right-item">
                        <div class="right-icon-wrap">
                          <i class="fas fa-person-circle-question" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="right-content">
                          <strong>Right Re: Automated Decisions</strong>
                          <p>Request human review of significant automated decisions, including risk assessment, fraud flagging, or account restrictions.</p>
                        </div>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">How to Exercise Your Rights</h3>
                  <p>You can submit a data subject request through the Privacy Settings section of your ZenoPay account dashboard, or by emailing <strong>privacy@zenopay.com</strong>. We will respond within 30 days (or within the period required by applicable law). We may ask you to verify your identity before processing your request.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Right to Complain</h3>
                  <p>If you believe we have not handled your personal data appropriately, you have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority. We encourage you to contact us first at <strong>privacy@zenopay.com</strong> so we can attempt to resolve your concern directly.</p>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 8: Data Retention -->
              <section id="section-8" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-8-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">8</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Storage Periods</p>
                    <h2 id="section-8-title" class="section-title">Data Retention</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected, or as required by applicable legal, regulatory, and contractual obligations.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Retention Periods by Category</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li><strong>Transaction records:</strong> A minimum of 7 years from the transaction date, in compliance with financial reporting and anti-money laundering regulations.</li>
                    <li><strong>KYC / identity verification data:</strong> For the duration of the account relationship, plus 5 years after account closure, or longer if required by applicable law.</li>
                    <li><strong>Account information:</strong> For the lifetime of your account, plus a post-closure period of up to 7 years for audit and dispute resolution purposes.</li>
                    <li><strong>Communication &amp; support records:</strong> Up to 3 years from last contact to support quality assurance and complaint handling obligations.</li>
                    <li><strong>Marketing consent records:</strong> Until withdrawal of consent, plus a reasonable period for documentation purposes.</li>
                    <li><strong>Security logs:</strong> Up to 90 days for operational logs, and up to 1 year for security event and audit logs.</li>
                  </ul>

                  <div class="callout-box info-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-circle-info callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Early Deletion Requests</strong>
                      Where you exercise your right to erasure, we will delete or anonymize personal data to the maximum extent possible. Data subject to mandatory statutory retention periods will be retained but access-restricted until the retention obligation expires.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 9: International Data Transfers -->
              <section id="section-9" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-9-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">9</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Cross-Border Processing</p>
                    <h2 id="section-9-title" class="section-title">International Data Transfers</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>ZenoPay operates globally. To provide the Services, we may transfer your personal data to countries other than your country of residence, including countries that may not provide the same level of data protection as your home jurisdiction.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">Safeguards for Cross-Border Transfers</h3>
                  <p>Whenever we transfer personal data internationally, we ensure that appropriate safeguards are in place. Depending on the destination country, these safeguards may include:</p>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) approved by the European Commission or equivalent regulatory body</li>
                    <li>Binding Corporate Rules for intra-group transfers</li>
                    <li>Transfers to countries with an adequacy decision from the relevant data protection authority</li>
                    <li>Specific contractual protections agreed with sub-processors</li>
                  </ul>

                  <div class="callout-box info-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-globe callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Primary Data Infrastructure</strong>
                      ZenoPay's primary data infrastructure is hosted in data centres located within the European Economic Area (EEA). Data residency options may be available for enterprise customers. Contact your account manager for details.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 10: Children's Privacy -->
              <section id="section-10" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-10-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">10</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Age Restrictions</p>
                    <h2 id="section-10-title" class="section-title">Children's Privacy</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>ZenoPay's Services are intended exclusively for adults aged 18 and over, or the age of majority in your jurisdiction. We do not knowingly collect, process, or retain personal data from individuals below the minimum age threshold.</p>

                  <div class="callout-box warning-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Underage Users</strong>
                      If we discover that we have inadvertently collected personal data from a person below the minimum age, we will immediately delete that data and close the associated account. If you believe a minor has registered for our Services, please contact us at <strong>privacy@zenopay.com</strong> immediately.
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <p>We do not direct our marketing, advertising, or communications toward individuals under the age of 18. Our registration flow includes age verification steps to minimise the risk of underage sign-ups.</p>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 11: Changes to This Policy -->
              <section id="section-11" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-11-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">11</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Policy Updates</p>
                    <h2 id="section-11-title" class="section-title">Changes to This Policy</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time as our Services evolve, as new regulatory requirements arise, or as we adopt improved privacy practices. The date at the top of this page reflects when the current version was last revised.</p>

                  <h3 class="subsection-title">How We Notify You</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li><strong>Material changes:</strong> We will provide at least 30 days' advance notice for changes that materially affect how we process your data. Notice will be sent by email to your registered address and displayed as an in-platform banner.</li>
                    <li><strong>Minor changes:</strong> Updates that do not materially affect your rights or our data practices (such as clarifications of existing language) will be published on this page with an updated revision date.</li>
                    <li><strong>Continued use:</strong> Your continued use of the Services after any policy update constitutes acceptance of the updated Privacy Policy. If you do not agree to a material change, you may close your account before the change takes effect.</li>
                  </ul>

                  <div class="callout-box info-callout">
                    <i class="fas fa-bell callout-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="callout-content">
                      <strong>Stay Informed</strong>
                      We recommend reviewing this Privacy Policy periodically. All previous versions of this policy are archived and available upon request by contacting our Privacy Team.
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </section>

              <!-- Section 12: Contact Us -->
              <section id="section-12" class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="section-12-title">
                <div class="section-header">
                  <span class="section-number">12</span>
                  <div>
                    <p class="section-kicker">Get in Touch</p>
                    <h2 id="section-12-title" class="section-title">Contact Us</h2>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="section-body">
                  <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, wish to exercise your data subject rights, or need to report a privacy concern, please reach out through the appropriate channel below.</p>

                  <div class="contact-cards-grid">
                    <div class="contact-card">
                      <div class="contact-card-icon-wrap">
                        <i class="fas fa-shield-halved" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                      </div>
